for unmodified noncommercial use, but the promotion condition in section 3
still applies. Making a modified version also requires the support payment
in section 4.

3. Required public promotion

Before your first operational use or redistribution under this license,
publish at least one publicly accessible acknowledgment that:

  (a) names POW and harnakam;
  (b) links to https://github.com/harnakam/POW; and
  (c) briefly and truthfully states that you use, redistribute, or modify POW.

You choose the medium, such as a public README, website, article, or social
post. One published acknowledgment covers your continuing use and multiple
versions; repeated promotional posts are not required.
No positive review, star, rating, endorsement, account on a particular
service, or disclosure of private project information is required.

For example: "We use POW by harnakam: https://github.com/harnakam/POW".

4. Required support payment for modifications

If you make a modified version of the Software, you must make one monetary
support payment to the Licensor before using or redistributing that
modified version. You choose the amount: any positive amount accepted by
the agreed payment method satisfies this condition. Zero does not.

The payment is required once per derivative project you maintain, not for
every edit, commit, release, installation, or copy. Subsequent revisions
of that same derivative project do not require another support payment.
Using an unchanged modified version received from someone else does not
itself require a payment under this section; making your own modifications
does. Retain your payment receipt or other acknowledgment privately.

Modifications mean changes to the Software's code, Skill instructions,
prompts, or documentation. Selecting or installing existing Skills, supplying
ordinary runtime arguments or project configuration, and creating unrelated
work with the Software do not by themselves count as modifications.

Contact the Licensor through the project repository to arrange a receiving
method. This license does not invent a payment address or authorize an
agent or installer to send money for you. A support payment is not a
commercial license and does not replace section 5.

5. Paid commercial permission

Commercial use requires a separate written commercial license from the
